# Idea: A Chime on Each Match

Raised by a tester in week 3. Rejected.

The idea was a short tone on each match and a longer one on a win, made with Web Audio so there would be no sound files. Two testers liked it in a quick trial.

It was rejected because the game is meant to be silent, so it can be played anywhere without surprising anyone, and feedback stays visual and announced. A mute switch was suggested as a compromise and rejected too, because it adds a setting to explain.

Status: rejected. Kept here so the idea isn't raised again without this context.
# Tryout: Card Flip Animation

What we tried for revealing cards.

A 3D `rotateY` flip looked nice on the laptop but stuttered on the old Android phone with the 16 by 16 board, and the back face sometimes flashed through. A quick scale and opacity change was smooth everywhere and kept the face readable during the change.

Worked: transform and opacity only, no layout properties. Didn't work: 3D flips with `backface-visibility` on large boards.
import { expect, test } from './browser-test.ts';
import { loadFixedBoard, exportedSnapshot } from './game-fixture.ts';

const COLOR_VECTOR = {
  page: 'rgb(9, 11, 20)',
  panel: 'rgb(20, 24, 39)',
